# Line endings.
#
# The repository stores LF for every text file. Without this, what gets recorded
# depends on whoever committed and how their Git happened to be configured, and
# a clone on another platform then shows every line of every file as changed.
#
# eol=lf is stated explicitly rather than left to each clone's core.autocrlf, so
# a checkout is byte-identical on Windows, Linux and macOS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell is the exception. These are run by Windows Task Scheduler and
# edited in Windows editors, where CRLF is what everything expects.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary. Never convert the bytes, never try to diff it as text.
*.png binary
